PASS launch failure: journal/spool/kill/revoke faults retain exact process identity and observation; no false stopped receipt
PASS pre-spawn authority recheck and concurrent session identity fencing
PASS exit dismissal: await receipt and finalizer; failure retains metadata and retryable close evidence
PASS recovery exclusion: exited runtime generation keeps its pending capture until own receipt
PASS launch place: a missing or non-folder cwd is refused before any launch effect
PASS runner availability: async, shared, cached per PATH for its TTL, one runner per launch
PASS a runner without modes records none
PASS a recorded failure keeps the kind of the real error, not its text
